cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ai-text-eval: an evaluation framework for AI-generated-text detection with conformal false-positive control"
message: "If you use this software in research, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - alias: YashToOp
repository-code: "https://github.com/YashToOp/Eval-AI"
url: "https://github.com/YashToOp/Eval-AI"
abstract: >-
  An open-source framework for evaluating machine-generated-text detectors.
  It implements the four signal families used by production detectors
  (perplexity, cross-model/Binoculars-style curvature, stylometry, and lexical
  forensics), and adds distribution-free false-positive control via split and
  multiscale conformal prediction, ternary Human/AI/Mixed verdicts with
  mandatory abstention, span-level attribution with change-point detection,
  Unicode homoglyph defenses, adversarial robustness evaluation, and
  per-subgroup false-positive-rate reporting. Designed around the finding that
  the operative risk in this domain is false positives concentrated in
  identifiable groups of writers, rather than aggregate accuracy.
keywords:
  - AI text detection
  - machine-generated text
  - large language models
  - conformal prediction
  - false positive rate
  - stylometry
  - adversarial robustness
  - algorithmic fairness
  - evaluation
license: MIT
version: 2.0.0
